# Tests — MSA Schedule 4 availability measurement

Assertion-based tests for `Availability`. Every branch of every exception
hierarchy is covered, and every threshold is tested on both sides:

  * L-2.6's "not less than 5 Business Days" at 4 and 5 clear Business Days;
  * L-2.5(b)'s "at least 60 minutes' notice" at 59 and 60 minutes;
  * L-2.6/L-4.5's 8-hour aggregate at 479, 480 and 481 minutes;
  * L-3.1's "not less than 99.90%" at exactly 99.90%;
  * L-2.3's rounding to two decimal places at the point where it decides
    whether a credit is due at all.

That last one is the trap with money attached. L-2.3 makes the Availability
Percentage the *rounded* figure, so an unrounded 99.8958% is an Availability
Percentage of 99.90%, the Service Level is met, and L-4.1 never engages. One
more Unavailable Minute takes it to an unrounded 99.8935%, which rounds to
99.89%, and the Customer is owed 5% of the Monthly Service Charge. The two
tests `L2_3_RoundsUpToTheServiceLevel` and `L2_3_RoundsBelowTheServiceLevel`
sit either side of that single minute.

The other trap with money attached is the L-4.5 interface. `excluded_minutes`
is the L-2.5 defined term as L-4.5 leaves it, so the Scheduled Maintenance
excess is not in it and cannot be charged twice; the pre-L-4.5 figure is
derived by the scope and reported as `excluded_minutes_before_l4_5`. The
`CE0010_` tests pin that, on the facts of CE-0010 and on the invariant it
turns on.

> Using Availability

## L2_1_ThirtyOneDayMonth

L-2.1: the denominator is the calendar month, so January has 44,640 minutes.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_1_ThirtyOneDayMonth:
  output r content Availability.MeasurementPeriod

scope TestL2_1_ThirtyOneDayMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.MeasurementPeriod with {
      -- period_start: |2025-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.period_end = |2025-01-31|
  assertion r.total_minutes = 44640
```

## L2_1_ShortMonth

L-2.1: February 2025 has 28 days, so 40,320 minutes.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_1_ShortMonth:
  output r content Availability.MeasurementPeriod

scope TestL2_1_ShortMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.MeasurementPeriod with {
      -- period_start: |2025-02-01|
    }
  assertion r.period_end = |2025-02-28|
  assertion r.total_minutes = 40320
```

## L2_1_LeapFebruary

L-2.1: February 2024 has 29 days, so 41,760 minutes. The denominator must be
read off the calendar and not assumed.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_1_LeapFebruary:
  output r content Availability.MeasurementPeriod

scope TestL2_1_LeapFebruary:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.MeasurementPeriod with {
      -- period_start: |2024-02-15|
    }
  assertion r.period_end = |2024-02-29|
  assertion r.total_minutes = 41760
```

## L2_2_Available

L-2.2: a well-formed request answered at the documented endpoint within the
latency threshold.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_2_Available:
  output r content Availability.RequestAvailable

scope TestL2_2_Available:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.RequestAvailable with {
      -- is_well_formed: true
      -- responded_at_documented_endpoint: true
      -- responded_within_latency_threshold: true
    }
  assertion r.is_available = true
```

## L2_2_LatencyBreach

L-2.2: a response outside the latency threshold is not Available.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_2_LatencyBreach:
  output r content Availability.RequestAvailable

scope TestL2_2_LatencyBreach:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.RequestAvailable with {
      -- is_well_formed: true
      -- responded_at_documented_endpoint: true
      -- responded_within_latency_threshold: false
    }
  assertion r.is_available = false
```

## L2_2_WrongEndpoint

L-2.2: the response must come at the Service's documented endpoint.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_2_WrongEndpoint:
  output r content Availability.RequestAvailable

scope TestL2_2_WrongEndpoint:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.RequestAvailable with {
      -- is_well_formed: true
      -- responded_at_documented_endpoint: false
      -- responded_within_latency_threshold: true
    }
  assertion r.is_available = false
```

## L2_2_MalformedRequest

L-2.2 speaks of a well-formed request, so a malformed one does not establish
availability.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_2_MalformedRequest:
  output r content Availability.RequestAvailable

scope TestL2_2_MalformedRequest:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.RequestAvailable with {
      -- is_well_formed: false
      -- responded_at_documented_endpoint: true
      -- responded_within_latency_threshold: true
    }
  assertion r.is_available = false
```

## L2_6_FiveBusinessDaysNotice

L-2.6: notice of exactly 5 clear Business Days is "not less than 5", so the
window is Scheduled Maintenance.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_FiveBusinessDaysNotice:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow

scope TestL2_6_FiveBusinessDaysNotice:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow with {
      -- is_maintenance: true
      -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
      -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-02-28|; |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|; |2025-03-10|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.business_days_notice = 5
  assertion r.is_scheduled_maintenance = true
```

## L2_6_FourBusinessDaysNotice

L-2.6: one Business Day less and the window is not Scheduled Maintenance at
all, so its minutes are not Excluded Minutes under L-2.5(a).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_FourBusinessDaysNotice:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow

scope TestL2_6_FourBusinessDaysNotice:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow with {
      -- is_maintenance: true
      -- notified_at: |2025-03-03|
      -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-02-28|; |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|; |2025-03-10|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.business_days_notice = 4
  assertion r.is_scheduled_maintenance = false
```

## L2_6_NotMaintenanceAtAll

L-2.6 qualifies maintenance. An ordinary outage with the same dates is not
Scheduled Maintenance however much notice happens to precede it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_NotMaintenanceAtAll:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow

scope TestL2_6_NotMaintenanceAtAll:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenanceWindow with {
      -- is_maintenance: false
      -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
      -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-02-28|; |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|; |2025-03-10|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.business_days_notice = 5
  assertion r.is_scheduled_maintenance = false
```

## L2_5_NoLimbApplies

L-2.5: an outage answering to none of the five limbs yields no Excluded
Minutes.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_5_NoLimbApplies:
  output r content Availability.ExcludedMinutes

scope TestL2_5_NoLimbApplies:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ExcludedMinutes with {
      -- minutes: 120
      -- is_scheduled_maintenance: false
      -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
      -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
      -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
      -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
      -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
    }
  assertion r.limb_a_scheduled_maintenance = false
  assertion r.limb_b_emergency_maintenance = false
  assertion r.limb_c_force_majeure = false
  assertion r.limb_d_customer_act = false
  assertion r.limb_e_suspension = false
  assertion r.is_excluded = false
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 0
```

## L2_5_LimbA

L-2.5(a): Scheduled Maintenance.

