## L2_5_TwoLimbsAtOnce

L-2.5's limbs are alternatives, not exceptions: an outage that answers to two
of them is excluded once, not twice.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_5_TwoLimbsAtOnce:
  output r content Availability.ExcludedMinutes

scope TestL2_5_TwoLimbsAtOnce:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ExcludedMinutes with {
      -- minutes: 200
      -- is_scheduled_maintenance: false
      -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
      -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
      -- force_majeure_event_certified: true
      -- outage_attributable_to_customer: true
      -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
    }
  assertion r.limb_c_force_majeure = true
  assertion r.limb_d_customer_act = true
  assertion r.is_excluded = true
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 200
```

## L2_6_AggregateJustUnderEightHours

L-2.6/L-4.5: 479 minutes of Scheduled Maintenance across two windows is under
the 8-hour ceiling, so there is no excess and all of it stays excluded.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_AggregateJustUnderEightHours:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenance

scope TestL2_6_AggregateJustUnderEightHours:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenance with {
      -- outages: [
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 239
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
             -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           };
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 240
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
             -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           }
         ]
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.cap_minutes = 480
  assertion r.aggregate_minutes = 479
  assertion r.excess_minutes = 0
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 479
```

## L2_6_AggregateExactlyEightHours

L-4.5 bites where Scheduled Maintenance "exceeds" 8 hours, which is strict, so
exactly 480 minutes produces no excess.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_AggregateExactlyEightHours:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenance

scope TestL2_6_AggregateExactlyEightHours:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenance with {
      -- outages: [
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 240
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
             -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           };
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 240
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-02-28|
             -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           }
         ]
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.aggregate_minutes = 480
  assertion r.excess_minutes = 0
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 480
```

