## L2_6_UnnotifiedWindowIsNotInTheAggregate

L-2.6: a maintenance window notified only 4 Business Days in advance is not
Scheduled Maintenance, so its minutes never enter the 8-hour aggregate — and
they are not Excluded Minutes either.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_6_UnnotifiedWindowIsNotInTheAggregate:
  output r content Availability.ScheduledMaintenance

scope TestL2_6_UnnotifiedWindowIsNotInTheAggregate:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ScheduledMaintenance with {
      -- outages: [
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 600
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-03-03|
             -- window_start: |2025-03-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           }
         ]
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-03-03|; |2025-03-04|; |2025-03-05|;
           |2025-03-06|; |2025-03-07|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.aggregate_minutes = 0
  assertion r.excess_minutes = 0
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 0
```

## L2_4_ExcludedMinutesComeOff

L-2.4: Unavailable Minutes are the minutes not Available less the Excluded
Minutes. With no maintenance overrun, the L-2.4 base case governs.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_4_ExcludedMinutesComeOff:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL2_4_ExcludedMinutesComeOff:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 43200
      -- minutes_not_available: 1000
      -- excluded_minutes: 600
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 400
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.07
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```

## L4_5_ExcessCountsAsUnavailable

L-4.5, as an exception to L-2.4: the same 600 minutes that L-2.5 would have
excluded on its own terms, but with 120 of them beyond the 8-hour aggregate.
L-4.5 withdraws those 120 from the exclusion, so the Excluded Minutes are 480,
and returns them to the count: Unavailable Minutes are 520 rather than 400 and
the Availability Percentage falls from 99.07% to 98.80%. The 480 is what a
caller passes as `excluded_minutes`, because that is what the defined term is
worth once L-4.5 has spoken; the scope reconstructs the 600 itself.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL4_5_ExcessCountsAsUnavailable:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL4_5_ExcessCountsAsUnavailable:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 43200
      -- minutes_not_available: 1000
      -- excluded_minutes: 480
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 120
    }
  assertion r.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 600
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 520
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 98.80
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```

## CE0010_TheExcessIsChargedOnceOnly

CE-0010's own facts: January 2026 (44,640 minutes), 600 whole minutes not
Available, all of them inside properly notified Scheduled Maintenance windows
totalling 10 hours. L-4.5 fixes the excess at 120 minutes and the Excluded
Minutes at 480. L-2.4 gives 600 − 480 = 120 Unavailable Minutes and L-2.3
gives 99.73%, which falls in L-4.1 band (a) at 5% of the Monthly Service
Charge. Charging the excess twice would give 240 minutes and 99.46%, which is
band (b) at 10% — the defect this test exists to keep out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCE0010_TheExcessIsChargedOnceOnly:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestCE0010_TheExcessIsChargedOnceOnly:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 44640
      -- minutes_not_available: 600
      -- excluded_minutes: 480
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 120
    }
  assertion r.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 600
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 120
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.73
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```

## CE0010_ExcludedMinutesMeanTheSameThingEitherWay

The interface property CE-0010 turned on: `excluded_minutes` means the L-2.5
defined term whether or not Scheduled Maintenance overran, so the excess can
never be charged on top of it. Two runs over the same 600 minutes not
Available and the same 480 Excluded Minutes — one where 480 minutes of
maintenance stayed inside the 8-hour aggregate and 120 minutes were never
excluded at all, one where 600 minutes of maintenance overran the aggregate by
120 — must give the same 120 Unavailable Minutes, because on both sets of
facts exactly 480 minutes are excluded. Only the reconstructed pre-L-4.5
figure differs, and it is derived rather than supplied.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCE0010_ExcludedMinutesMeanTheSameThingEitherWay:
  output without_excess content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage
  output with_excess content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestCE0010_ExcludedMinutesMeanTheSameThingEitherWay:
  definition without_excess equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 44640
      -- minutes_not_available: 600
      -- excluded_minutes: 480
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  definition with_excess equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 44640
      -- minutes_not_available: 600
      -- excluded_minutes: 480
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 120
    }
  assertion without_excess.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 480
  assertion without_excess.unavailable_minutes = 120
  assertion with_excess.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 600
  assertion with_excess.unavailable_minutes = 120
```

## L3_1_ExactlyAtTheServiceLevel

L-3.1: "not less than 99.90%" is inclusive, so an Availability Percentage of
exactly 99.90% meets the Service Level. A 30-day month with 43.2 Unavailable
Minutes would be exactly 99.90%; 43 minutes rounds to 99.90% from above.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL3_1_ExactlyAtTheServiceLevel:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL3_1_ExactlyAtTheServiceLevel:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 43200
      -- minutes_not_available: 43
      -- excluded_minutes: 0
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.90
  assertion r.meets_service_level = true
```

## L2_3_RoundsUpToTheServiceLevel

L-2.3: 45 Unavailable Minutes in a 30-day month is an unrounded 99.895833%,
which rounds to an Availability Percentage of 99.90%. The Service Level is met
and L-4.1 never engages, because the defined term is the rounded figure.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_3_RoundsUpToTheServiceLevel:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL2_3_RoundsUpToTheServiceLevel:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 43200
      -- minutes_not_available: 45
      -- excluded_minutes: 0
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 45
  assertion r.availability_percentage_unrounded < 99.90
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.90
  assertion r.meets_service_level = true
```

## L2_3_RoundsBelowTheServiceLevel

L-2.3: one further Unavailable Minute gives an unrounded 99.893518%, which
rounds to 99.89% — below the Service Level, and inside L-4.1 band (a). One
minute is the whole distance between nothing and 5% of the Monthly Service
Charge.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_3_RoundsBelowTheServiceLevel:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL2_3_RoundsBelowTheServiceLevel:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 43200
      -- minutes_not_available: 46
      -- excluded_minutes: 0
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 46
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.89
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```

## L2_3_RoundingIsNotTruncation

L-2.3 rounds to two decimal places rather than truncating: an unrounded
99.8958% is 99.90%, not 99.89%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_3_RoundingIsNotTruncation:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL2_3_RoundingIsNotTruncation:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 40320
      -- minutes_not_available: 42
      -- excluded_minutes: 0
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.availability_percentage_unrounded < 99.90
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.90
  assertion r.meets_service_level = true
```

## L2_3_PerfectMonth

L-2.3: no Unavailable Minutes gives 100.00%.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL2_3_PerfectMonth:
  output r content Availability.AvailabilityPercentage

scope TestL2_3_PerfectMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.AvailabilityPercentage with {
      -- total_minutes: 44640
      -- minutes_not_available: 0
      -- excluded_minutes: 0
      -- scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes: 0
    }
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 0
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 100.00
  assertion r.meets_service_level = true
```

## Integration_MaintenanceOverrun

The whole chain over one Measurement Period: April 2025 (43,200 minutes) with
600 minutes of properly notified Scheduled Maintenance, 100 minutes of
certified Force Majeure and 200 minutes of plain outage. L-2.5's limbs exclude
700 minutes on their own terms; L-2.6's aggregate ceiling is exceeded by 120,
so L-4.5 withdraws those 120 from the exclusion — the Excluded Minutes for the
period are 580 — and returns them to Unavailable Minutes, giving 320 rather
than 200, and 99.26%. The excess moves the figure exactly once.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestIntegration_MaintenanceOverrun:
  output r content Availability.ServiceAvailability

scope TestIntegration_MaintenanceOverrun:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ServiceAvailability with {
      -- period_start: |2025-04-01|
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-03-25|; |2025-03-26|; |2025-03-27|;
           |2025-03-28|; |2025-03-31|
         ]
      -- outages: [
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 600
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-03-24|
             -- window_start: |2025-04-01|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           };
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 100
             -- is_maintenance: false
             -- notified_at: |2025-04-10|
             -- window_start: |2025-04-10|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: true
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           };
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 200
             -- is_maintenance: false
             -- notified_at: |2025-04-20|
             -- window_start: |2025-04-20|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           }
         ]
    }
  assertion r.total_minutes = 43200
  assertion r.minutes_not_available = 900
  assertion r.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 700
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 580
  assertion r.scheduled_maintenance_aggregate_minutes = 600
  assertion r.scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes = 120
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 320
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.26
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```

## Integration_NoOverrun

The same month with 480 rather than 600 minutes of Scheduled Maintenance: the
aggregate is exactly at the ceiling, nothing is returned to Unavailable
Minutes, and the Service Level is still missed but by less.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestIntegration_NoOverrun:
  output r content Availability.ServiceAvailability

scope TestIntegration_NoOverrun:
  definition r equals
    output of Availability.ServiceAvailability with {
      -- period_start: |2025-04-01|
      -- business_day_calendar: [
           |2025-03-25|; |2025-03-26|; |2025-03-27|;
           |2025-03-28|; |2025-03-31|
         ]
      -- outages: [
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 480
             -- is_maintenance: true
             -- notified_at: |2025-03-24|
             -- window_start: |2025-04-01|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           };
           Availability.Outage {
             -- minutes: 200
             -- is_maintenance: false
             -- notified_at: |2025-04-20|
             -- window_start: |2025-04-20|
             -- is_emergency_maintenance: false
             -- emergency_notice_minutes: 0
             -- force_majeure_event_certified: false
             -- outage_attributable_to_customer: false
             -- is_suspension_under_clause_9: false
           }
         ]
    }
  assertion r.minutes_not_available = 680
  assertion r.excluded_minutes_before_l4_5 = 480
  assertion r.excluded_minutes = 480
  assertion r.scheduled_maintenance_excess_minutes = 0
  assertion r.unavailable_minutes = 200
  assertion r.availability_percentage = 99.54
  assertion r.meets_service_level = false
```
